; Hand-assembled Cancun counter. PCs and operands are hex.
0000 34 CALLVALUE ; Nonpayable guard for every entry and fallback.
0001 6100ad PUSH2 0x00ad ; Target reject.
0004 57 JUMPI ; Branch to reject.
0005 6004 PUSH1 0x04 ; Minimum selector size.
0007 36 CALLDATASIZE ; Read supplied byte count.
0008 10 LT ; Reject a selector shorter than four bytes.
0009 6100ad PUSH2 0x00ad ; Target reject.
000c 57 JUMPI ; Branch to reject.
000d 5f PUSH0 ; Selector word offset.
000e 35 CALLDATALOAD ; Read selector and the first argument prefix.
000f 60e0 PUSH1 0xe0 ; Discard the low 224 bits.
0011 1c SHR ; Extract the four-byte selector.
0012 5f PUSH0 ; Memory offset 0.
0013 52 MSTORE ; Save selector for the three dispatch comparisons.
0014 5f PUSH0 ; Memory offset 0.
0015 51 MLOAD ; Load selector for increment.
0016 637cf5dab0 PUSH4 0x7cf5dab0 ; Selector of increment(uint256).
001b 14 EQ ; Match the complete selector.
001c 61003c PUSH2 0x003c ; Target increment.
001f 57 JUMPI ; Branch to increment.
0020 5f PUSH0 ; Memory offset 0.
0021 51 MLOAD ; Load selector for decrement.
0022 633a9ebefd PUSH4 0x3a9ebefd ; Selector of decrement(uint256).
0027 14 EQ ; Match the complete selector.
0028 610074 PUSH2 0x0074 ; Target decrement.
002b 57 JUMPI ; Branch to decrement.
002c 5f PUSH0 ; Memory offset 0.
002d 51 MLOAD ; Load selector for get.
002e 636d4ce63c PUSH4 0x6d4ce63c ; Selector of get().
0033 14 EQ ; Match the complete selector.
0034 61009b PUSH2 0x009b ; Target get.
0037 57 JUMPI ; Branch to get.
0038 6100ad PUSH2 0x00ad ; Target reject.
003b 56 JUMP ; Branch to reject.
003c 5b JUMPDEST ; Begin increment.
003d 6024 PUSH1 0x24 ; Four selector bytes plus one 32-byte argument.
003f 36 CALLDATASIZE ; Trailing calldata is permitted.
0040 10 LT ; Reject a short argument head.
0041 6100ad PUSH2 0x00ad ; Target reject.
0044 57 JUMPI ; Branch to reject.
0045 6004 PUSH1 0x04 ; First argument offset.
0047 35 CALLDATALOAD ; Decode the full uint256 argument.
0048 6020 PUSH1 0x20 ; Memory offset 32.
004a 52 MSTORE ; Save argument n.
004b 5f PUSH0 ; Count is storage slot zero.
004c 54 SLOAD ; Read current count c.
004d 5f PUSH0 ; Memory offset 0.
004e 52 MSTORE ; Save current count c.
004f 5f PUSH0 ; Memory offset 0.
0050 51 MLOAD ; Load c for addition.
0051 6020 PUSH1 0x20 ; Memory offset 32.
0053 51 MLOAD ; Load n for addition.
0054 01 ADD ; Compute sum modulo 2^256, before the overflow guard.
0055 6040 PUSH1 0x40 ; Memory offset 64.
0057 52 MSTORE ; Save sum s.
0058 5f PUSH0 ; Memory offset 0.
0059 51 MLOAD ; Overflow comparison right operand c.
005a 6040 PUSH1 0x40 ; Memory offset 64.
005c 51 MLOAD ; Overflow comparison left operand s.
005d 10 LT ; Overflow exactly when s is less than c.
005e 6100ad PUSH2 0x00ad ; Target reject.
0061 57 JUMPI ; Branch to reject.
0062 6001 PUSH1 0x01 ; Limit is storage slot one.
0064 54 SLOAD ; Bound comparison right operand limit.
0065 6040 PUSH1 0x40 ; Memory offset 64.
0067 51 MLOAD ; Bound comparison left operand s.
0068 11 GT ; Reject s greater than limit, allowing equality.
0069 6100ad PUSH2 0x00ad ; Target reject.
006c 57 JUMPI ; Branch to reject.
006d 6040 PUSH1 0x40 ; Memory offset 64.
006f 51 MLOAD ; Return and store the checked sum.
0070 6100a2 PUSH2 0x00a2 ; Target save.
0073 56 JUMP ; Branch to save.
0074 5b JUMPDEST ; Begin decrement.
0075 6024 PUSH1 0x24 ; Four selector bytes plus one 32-byte argument.
0077 36 CALLDATASIZE ; Trailing calldata is permitted.
0078 10 LT ; Reject a short argument head.
0079 6100ad PUSH2 0x00ad ; Target reject.
007c 57 JUMPI ; Branch to reject.
007d 6004 PUSH1 0x04 ; First argument offset.
007f 35 CALLDATALOAD ; Decode the full uint256 argument.
0080 6020 PUSH1 0x20 ; Memory offset 32.
0082 52 MSTORE ; Save argument n.
0083 5f PUSH0 ; Count is storage slot zero.
0084 54 SLOAD ; Read current count c.
0085 5f PUSH0 ; Memory offset 0.
0086 52 MSTORE ; Save current count c.
0087 5f PUSH0 ; Memory offset 0.
0088 51 MLOAD ; Underflow comparison right operand c.
0089 6020 PUSH1 0x20 ; Memory offset 32.
008b 51 MLOAD ; Underflow comparison left operand n.
008c 11 GT ; Reject n greater than c, allowing equality.
008d 6100ad PUSH2 0x00ad ; Target reject.
0090 57 JUMPI ; Branch to reject.
0091 6020 PUSH1 0x20 ; Memory offset 32.
0093 51 MLOAD ; Subtraction right operand n.
0094 5f PUSH0 ; Memory offset 0.
0095 51 MLOAD ; Subtraction left operand c.
0096 03 SUB ; Compute c minus n only after the underflow guard.
0097 6100a2 PUSH2 0x00a2 ; Target save.
009a 56 JUMP ; Branch to save.
009b 5b JUMPDEST ; Begin get.
009c 5f PUSH0 ; Count is storage slot zero.
009d 54 SLOAD ; Return count without a storage write.
009e 6100a6 PUSH2 0x00a6 ; Target return.
00a1 56 JUMP ; Branch to return.
00a2 5b JUMPDEST ; Begin save.
00a3 80 DUP1 ; Preserve the result for return.
00a4 5f PUSH0 ; Only update the count slot.
00a5 55 SSTORE ; Commit the checked count.
00a6 5b JUMPDEST ; Begin return.
00a7 5f PUSH0 ; Memory offset 0.
00a8 52 MSTORE ; Encode the uint256 result in memory.
00a9 6020 PUSH1 0x20 ; Return exactly one ABI word.
00ab 5f PUSH0 ; Return from memory offset zero.
00ac f3 RETURN ; Finish successfully.
00ad 5b JUMPDEST ; Begin reject.
00ae 5f PUSH0 ; Empty revert length.
00af 5f PUSH0 ; Empty revert offset.
00b0 fd REVERT ; Reject and roll back all state changes.
